  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN.\n\nYou are allowed to perform the following operation on it any number of times:\n\n\nChoose an index iii such that 1&lt;i&lt;N1 \\lt i \\lt N1&lt;i&lt;N, and any integer XXX (XXX can be negative).\nThen, modify the array as follows:\n\nSubtract XXX from Ai−1A_{i-1}Ai−1​ (that is, Ai−1→Ai−1−XA_{i-1} \\to A_{i-1} - XAi−1​→Ai−1​−X)\nAdd 2X2X2X to AiA_iAi​ (that is, Ai→Ai+2XA_i \\to A_i + 2XAi​→Ai​+2X)\nSubtract XXX from Ai+1A_{i+1}Ai+1​ (that is, Ai+1→Ai+1−XA_{i+1} \\to A_{i+1} - XAi+1​→Ai+1​−X)\n\n\nYour task is to find the minimum number of operations required to convert the array AAA into a palindrome†^\\dagger†.\n\nIf it is not possible to do so, output −1-1−1 instead.\n\n†^\\dagger† An integer array AAA of length NNN is called a palindrome iff Ai=AN+1−iA_i = A_{N+1-i}Ai​=AN+1−i​ for every i=1,2,3,…,Ni = 1, 2, 3, \\ldots, Ni=1,2,3,…,N.\n\nFor example, [−3,35,35,−3][-3, 35, 35, -3][−3,35,35,−3] is a palindrome, while [12,21][12, 21][12,21] is not.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two line of input.\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN, the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the minimum number of operations required to make the array AAA a palindrome.\n\nIf it is not possible to do so, output −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "3≤N≤4⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 4 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤4⋅105",
      "−106≤Ai≤106-10^6 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^6−106≤Ai​≤106",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 4⋅1054 \\cdot 10^54⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
